          "path": "_m/u/1/1/3/fortress-of-mimoyecques-wp/vertical-photographic-reconnai.jpg",
          "filename": "Vertical photographic-reconnaissance aerial of Mimoyecques.jpg",
          "caption": "Vertical photographic-reconnaissance aerial showing the German secret weapon (V3) site at Mimoyecques, near Marquise, France, after the daylight attack by aircraft of Bomber Command on 6 July 1944. Many craters from previous attacks by Allied aircraft pit the surrounding area. The large bomb craters were caused by 12,000-lb \"Tallboy\" deep-penetration bombs dropped by No. 617 Squadron RAF, which was led for the last time on 6 July by Wing Commander G L Cheshire VC.",
          "alt": "Vertical photographic-reconnaissance aerial showing the German secret weapon (V3) site at Mimoyecques, near Marquise, France, after the daylight attack by aircraft of Bomber Command on 6 July 1944. Many craters from previous attacks by Allied aircraft pit the surrounding area. The large bomb craters were caused by 12,000-lb \"Tallboy\" deep-penetration bombs dropped by No. 617 Squadron RAF, which was led for the last time on 6 July by Wing Commander G L Cheshire VC.",
          "width": 800,
          "height": 660,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "Donaghue (Flt Lt): No. 541 Squadron RAF",
